// WHICH WAY AN NPC STANDS BEFORE ANYTHING HAS HAPPENED TO IT.
//
// A map's NPC section carries a coord and a type and nothing else - GameMap.loadNpcs constructs the
// npc with no orientation - so every npc in the game spawns facing south, and there was no way to
// say otherwise. It only shows on an npc that never moves: a wanderrange=0 shopkeeper stands in
// whatever direction it spawned in until a player talks to it.
//
// The value is one of engine.constant's ^exact_north / ^exact_east / ^exact_south / ^exact_west,
// the same four the exactmove and direction procs use. -1, the default, leaves the npc alone - so
// this changes nothing for the 16,383 npcs that do not set it.
//
// Read by [ai_spawn,_] (npc/scripts/ai_spawn.rs2), which is the one trigger every npc runs on
// spawn. Deliberately NOT a type-specific [ai_spawn,vote_clerk]: ScriptProvider.getByTrigger
// resolves type before the wildcard and only ever runs ONE script, so an npc with its own ai_spawn
// silently stops getting %npc_start_coord and its combat xp multiplier.
[spawn_face]
type=int
default=-1
